# Generated artefacts, not sources. The print-test sheet comes from
# `npm run print-test`; label.pdf is what the documented curl example writes.
print-test-sheet*.pdf
/label.pdf

# Playwright: reports, traces, and the screenshots the panel specs write for
# looking at. All regenerated by `npm run test:e2e`; none is an input to anything.
/test-results/
/playwright-report/
/e2e/__screenshots__/

# Scratch from the brainstorming companion — mockups written to be looked at
# once, during one conversation. Same reasoning as the screenshots below.
/.superpowers/

# Screenshots taken to look at the interface during a review, kept beside the
# notes they support. Same reasoning as the line above and one more: these are
# megabytes of PNG whose whole job is to be read once, by the person who asked
# for them. The findings they evidence belong in a document; the pixels do not
# belong in the history.
/docs/ui-audit-*/

# The fake-camera video the scanner tests read is generated into the system
# temporary directory at launch, not into the repository — eight uncompressed
# frames is five megabytes, and it is derived from the engine in this repository,
# so committing it would store a slow copy of something the build can make.
